==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ine-pro|la}} {{recons|atro-ek|lang=ine-pro}}, from  {{etyl|ine-pro|la}} {{recons|h₁eh₂ter-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|eh₂ter-||fire|lang=ine-pro}} (whence Sanskrit {{term|अथर्वन्|tr=átharvan|lang=sa}} and Avestan {{term|𐬁𐬙𐬀𐬭𐬱||fire|tr=ātarš|lang=ae}}, see also Umbrian {{term||...|tr=atru|lang=xum}}, Oscan {{term||...|tr=Aadíriis|lang=osc}}, Irish {{term|áith||kiln|lang=ga}}.
 {{rfscript|Ital}}<!-- Umbrian and Oscan, above -->) + {{recons|h₃okʷ-||lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|h₃ekʷ-||eye; to see|lang=ine-pro}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/ˈa.troːks/|lang=la}}

